--- 
title: "stdlib.ini Tutorial"
author: IVANLI2412
date: 2026-11-23
abstract: INI file parsing with typed getters, set/merge/delete, and round-trip serialization.

# stdlib.ini Tutorial

INI configuration file parsing and manipulation.

## Functions
- `parse(text) -> INIDoc`: Parse INI text
- `get(doc, section, key, default?) -> str`: String value
- `get_int(doc, section, key, default?) -> int`: Integer (supports 0x, 0o, 0b)
- `get_float(doc, section, key, default?) -> float`: Float value
- `get_bool(doc, section, key, default?) -> bool`: Boolean (true/false, yes/no, on/off, 1/0)
- `set(doc, section, key, value) -> INIDoc`: Immutable set
- `delete(doc, section, key) -> INIDoc`: Delete key or section
- `to_string(doc) -> str`: Serialize to INI text
- `merge(doc1, doc2) -> INIDoc`: Merge (doc2 overrides)
- `sections(doc) -> list[str]`, `section_keys(doc, section) -> list[str]`

## Example
```lateralus
let doc = ini.parse("[db]\nhost=localhost\nport=5432\nssl=true\n")
ini.get(doc, "db", "host")        -- "localhost"
ini.get_int(doc, "db", "port")    -- 5432
ini.get_bool(doc, "db", "ssl")    -- true
```
